WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.117
You may hear more and more about agentic RAG.

00:00:03.117 --> 00:00:09.657
Classic RAG usually follows a direct flow: receive a question, retrieve evidence, build context,

00:00:09.657 --> 00:00:13.422
and generate an answer. Agentic RAG can make additional decisions.

00:00:13.422 --> 00:00:20.452
An agent might break a complex question into smaller parts, choose among multiple data sources,

00:00:20.452 --> 00:00:29.802
call different tools, inspect intermediate results, and decide whether another retrieval step is needed.

00:00:29.802 --> 00:00:35.577
[tts-break] That can be useful for multi-hop questions or tasks that span several systems.

00:00:35.577 --> 00:00:40.312
But agentic RAG does not remove the need to understand classic retrieval.

00:00:40.312 --> 00:00:46.942
The agent still depends on good data, useful chunks, embeddings, search, permissions, and evaluation.

00:00:46.942 --> 00:00:52.517
That is why this module teaches the classic pipeline first.

00:00:52.517 --> 00:00:57.632
Once you understand the basic architecture, agentic patterns become an extension rather than another black

00:00:57.632 --> 00:00:59.551
box.
